  "notes": "A new version of NovelOS is available. Download the latest version from https://novelos.studio/downloads and install it manually.",
  "release_notes": "## New\n\n- **Smart quotes and dashes.** Quotes you type in the Manuscript become curly quotes, and two hyphens become an em dash. Pasted text is left as it is. Turn it off in Settings > Editor & Typography > Smart Quotes and Dashes. Works on desktop and phone.\n- **Click to place on the Blueprint board.** Clicking a plot point, scene, character, place or lore item in the Blueprint sidebar now places it in the middle of the board. Dragging still works.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- **Read Aloud says the chapter number.** A chapter titled \"Chapter\" was read as just \"Chapter\". Read Aloud and audiobook export now say \"Chapter 1\", \"Chapter 2\" and so on, numbered the same way as your exported book.\n- **Scene breaks are a pause.** Read Aloud and audiobooks no longer say \"asterisk asterisk\" at a * * * scene break.\n- **Voice and speed changes apply right away.** Changing the voice or speed while Read Aloud plays now takes effect from the passage you are hearing.\n- **No more Mandarin-sounding replays.** Chapters recorded on 1.5.0 or 1.5.1 with the faulty voice are recorded again instead of replayed. ElevenLabs recordings are kept.\n- **Read Aloud keeps going in the background.** On a Mac, pressing Play and switching to another app could stall Read Aloud and audiobook export.\n- **Panels show words again.** In 1.5.2, Read Aloud settings, the voice picker and Muse tabs showed labels like editor.narration.enable. They now show proper text.\n- **Plot types match on phone and desktop.** Plot types set on the phone no longer show as Custom on the desktop.\n- **+ Add subtitle** puts the cursor in the new subtitle field.\n\n## Good to know\n\n- On 1.5.0 or later, NovelOS offers this update itself and installs it when you restart. On 1.4.2 or earlier, download it from novelos.studio/downloads.",
